    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Established in the 1950s by André Bazin, Joseph-Marie Lo Duca, and Jacques Doniol-Valcroze, France’s Cahiers du cinéma has been a bastion for international film criticism for decades. They’ve now unveiled their predictably stellar top 15 films of 2026 list."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Topping the list is Emmanuel Marre’s Cannes premiere A Man of His Time , which will get a 2027 U.S. release, as will their second pick: Alain Gomis’ Dao . Ryusuke Hamaguchi’s latest masterpiece All of a Sudden is also among the top 10 as is Marine Atlan’s incredible debut La Gradiva and two more Cannes premieres that deserved more love upon their initial bows: Arthur Harari’s The Unknown and Valeska Grisebach’s The Dreamed Adventure ."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Also among the top 15 is a trio of 2025 U.S. releases that opened in France this year: James L. Brooks’ maligned but fascinating Ella McCay , Kelly Reichardt’s The Mastermind , and Josh Safdie’s Marty Supreme ."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Check out the list below via their latest issue and click titles to see our reviews.",
